#
# Directories Bazel must not descend into when expanding a `//...` pattern.
#
# This is not an optimization. `bazel query //...` in presubmit.yml loads every BUILD file it
# finds, and these trees contain BUILD files that are not ours — a vendored dependency in
# .venv or node_modules carries its own, written against rulesets this workspace does not
# declare, and loading one fails the whole query with an error naming a file nobody here
# wrote. Same class of failure as the rules_go/Bazel 9 note in MODULE.bazel.
#
# LITERAL PATHS ONLY, relative to the workspace root. .bazelignore does not glob: a line
# reading `**/node_modules` matches a directory named exactly that and nothing else. Nested
# occurrences have to be listed, which is why the entries below are the root ones — a
# node_modules under apps/ needs its own line if pnpm ever installs there.

# Python virtualenv. Created by `uv sync`; carries an entire site-packages tree.
.venv

# Node. pnpm-workspace.yaml declares apps/*, libs/ts/* and sdk/typescript, so add those paths
# here too once the lockfile installs anything — today it declares no dependencies.
node_modules
.pnpm-store

# Cargo build output. The Rust workspace is built through rules_rust from source; a stale
# ./target from a direct `cargo build` is not an input to anything Bazel does.
target

# Nix and direnv.
.direnv
result

# Bazel's own convenience symlinks are ignored automatically, and `make clean-local` removes
# them, but .bazel-cache is a plain directory that .gitignore creates room for and Bazel would
# otherwise walk.
.bazel-cache
